analysisWe need to produce an assert statement corresponding to the comment:

```java
// @@@ If the result is not null, then the key was already present in the map before the operation.
```

We are inside method `public V put(K key, V value)`. The comment says: "If the result is not null, then the key was already present in the map before the operation."

The result is the return value of put: `\result`. The condition: if `\result != null` then the key was already present before the operation. How to express key was already present before the operation? There is a method `containsKey(Object key)` that checks presence. We need to refer to old state: before operation, the map may have contained the key. So we need to assert: `\result != null => \old(this.containsKey(key))`. Also maybe we need to assert that if result is null, then key was not present before. But comment only asserts the forward implication. So assert: `\result != null => \old(this.containsKey(key))`. That uses `\old`. Use `this.containsKey(key)` after operation? The comment says "key was already present in the map before the operation." So we need `\old(this.containsKey(key))`. So final assert:

```
assert \result != null => \old(this.containsKey(key));
```

Make sure syntax correct: parentheses maybe: `assert (\result != null) => \old(this.containsKey(key));`

