Method put returns V (previous value) or null. The assertion: if \result != null then the map already contained the key before the put.

We need to express "key was already present in the map before the operation". Use observer method containsKey? That's available: public boolean containsKey(Object key). Use old state: \old(this.containsKey(key)). So assert: (\result != null) => \old(this.containsKey(key))

But also note: if result is null, key may have been absent or present with previous null value. The spec only states implication for result not null. So we write:

assert (\result != null) => \old(this.containsKey(key));

